bool isPalindrome(std::string s) {
    int i = 0, j = (int)s.size() - 1;
    while (i < j) {
        while (i < j && !isalnum(s[i])) i++;
        while (i < j && !isalnum(s[j])) j--;
        if (tolower(s[i++]) != tolower(s[j--])) return false;
    }
    return true;
}
```
Two pointers walking inward, skipping anything non-alphanumeric, folding case before it compares. A palindrome is a claim that survives being read backwards. Here is another one: the Saudis lost 2-0 in Jakarta, having themselves put Argentina away 2-1. Start from either pointer, walk either direction, and the verdict is that Indonesia outclasses Argentina at soccer. That function never returns false.

